{title: O Sacred Head Now Wounded}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune PASSION CHORALE}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O [F]sacred [**]Head, now [G]woun[C]ded with [Am]grief and [E7]shame weighed [Am]down
Now [F]scornful[**]ly sur[G]roun[C]ded with [Am]thorns, Thine [E7]only [Am]crown
How [G]pale thou [F]art with [C]an[**]guish with [F]sore a[**]buse and [Am]scorn
How [G]does that [C]visage [D]lan[G]guish which [F]once was [G]bright as [C]morn.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
What [F]Thou, my [**]Lord, hast [G]suf[C]fered, t'was [Am]all for [E7]sinners' [Am]gain
Mine, [F]mine was [**]the trans[G]gres[C]sion but [Am]Thine the [E7]deadly [Am]pain
Lo, [G]here I [F]fall, my [C]Sa[**]viour ‘tis [F]I de[**]serve Thy [Am]place
Look [G]on me [C]with Thy [D]fa[G]vour vouch[F]safe to [G]me Thy [C]grace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
What [F]language [**]shall I [G]bor[C]row to [Am]thank thee, [E7]dearest [Am]Friend
For [F]this, thy [**]dying [G]sor[C]row, thy [Am]pity [E7]without [Am]end?
Oh, [G]make me [F]thine fo[C]re[**]ver and [F]should I [**]fainting [Am]be
Lord, [G]let me [C]never, [D]ne[G]ver out[F]live my [G]love to [C]thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Be [F]near when [**]I am [G]dy[C]ing, oh, [Am]show your [E7]cross to [Am]me
And [F]for my [**]rescue, [G]fly[C]ing, come, [Am]Lord, and [E7]set me [Am]free!
These [G]eyes, new [F]faith re[C]cei[**]ving from [F]Jesus [**]shall not [Am]move
